  "preamble": "Change of the voiceless velar stop [k] to the bilabial [p]. With plain /k/ it is rare; the clearest case is Eastern Romance, where Latin /k/ became /p/ before /t/ and in /ks/: Romanian opt, lapte, noapte and coapsă, Aromanian optu, lapti and noapti, and Dalmatian uapto 'eight'. The better-known labiovelar developments (PIE *kʷ > Greek and P-Celtic p, Latin aqua > Romanian apă) start from [kʷ], not plain [k], and are not filed here.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Labialization, Change of Place",
